    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49474" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tūrĭa</span></b> , ae,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river in</i> Hispania Tarraconensis, now <i>the
				Turia</i> or <i>Guadalaviar</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 6,
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sall. H. 2, 96, 6</span></i> Dietsch; 2, 18
			ib.—Called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tūrĭum</span></b> , ii,
			n., <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 3, 4, §
			20</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tūrĭensis</span></b> , e,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to Turia</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proelium (in the Sertorian war),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Balb. 2, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
